# The version Montana for Android shows, the way iOS shows its own: v<MARKETING> (<build>).
#
# While Android is catching up with iOS it shows its own build and the iOS build it goes to:
#   v1.0 (31 → 1277)   — the 31st Android build (the commits on main), on the way to iOS 1277.
# iOS 1277 is the frozen point shipped to TestFlight on 02.09 (iOS commit c181287d, «version 0.313, build 1277»).
#
# When Android does what iOS 1277 does, TARGET empties and BUILD becomes 1277: the app shows v1.0 (1277).
# From then on BUILD is the iOS build Android has reached, by the iOS changelog:
#   https://github.com/efir369999/montana_messenger/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
MARKETING=1.0
TARGET=1277
BUILD=
